      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Screenshots from the IMDb website. After Multi-Click is activated with double-tapping Shift , users can hover over an initial element and scroll the mouse wheel to generalize to equivalent elements."
    },
    {
      "path": "figures/zhang-multi-click-uist2025/figure-005-p004.png",
      "node": "1134:0",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        51.79800033569336,
        81.68592071533203,
        560.2100219726562,
        297.00799560546875
      ],
      "sha256": "cf9f6050daec4af4b6680b6e9ace27bff075779811182f76e0831e32d0411a09",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Overview of Multi-Click’s User Interface. The user can activate Multi-Click by double-tapping Shift and scroll to select the input elements to enter values. The generalized elements are highlighted in purple (a). The user can see selected elements in other tabs in the preview cards, where the selected elements are highlighted in blue (c). Then the user can enter values in the interactive data table (d) and calculate results for each term simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "path": "figures/zhang-multi-click-uist2025/figure-006-p006.png",
      "node": "1255:0",
      "page": 6,
      "bbox": [
        51.79800033569336,
        81.68751525878906,
        296.0375671386719,
        226.44900512695312
      ],
      "sha256": "6d5bb26843012064e7a3e3c289b2e74b9e90f66e2be6a29a5e15257f626a678f",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "A grouped bar chart compares average task completion time, with error bars and significance brackets. For Tasks 1, 2 and 3 respectively, Multi-Click averages 1:31, 1:31 and 0:47; manual completion averages 2:23, 2:59 and 2:59; Operator averages 13:31, 9:55 and 3:36 (minutes:seconds). Multi-Click is fastest in all three tasks. The exact means and standard deviations appear in Table 1. Asterisks mark p < 0.05 in Welch’s t-test."
    },
    {
      "path": "figures/zhang-multi-click-uist2025/figure-007-p007.png",
      "node": "1325:0",
      "page": 7,
      "bbox": [
        51.79800033569336,
        81.6852798461914,
        560.2044067382812,
        179.58799743652344
      ],
      "sha256": "0de9251e3ea87ca5a0c4911bec87de54603a6818b4d2b0b08d90799b9cc8f0e3",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Two horizontal stacked-bar panels show NASA-TLX response distributions for Multi-Click and Operator across mental demand, physical demand, hurriedness, perceived success, effort required, and stress/discouragement. Ratings run from 1 in dark red to 7 in dark blue; 1 indicates higher load, hurry, effort or stress and lower success. Multi-Click responses lean toward the favorable higher ratings across all six questions. Operator has more low ratings for hurriedness and more middle ratings for perceived success and effort. The clearest contrast is hurriedness: Operator has responses across ratings 1 through 7, including a large rating-1 segment, while Multi-Click responses are concentrated at 4 through 7."
    },
    {
